# Line-ending policy.
#
# The comparison harness feeds the mission and the interface notes to an agent
# byte-for-byte and asserts those bytes in tests. Git stores them as LF, but a
# Windows checkout with `core.autocrlf=true` used to materialise them as CRLF,
# so the byte assertions held on one machine's checkout and failed on a fresh
# one — a harness input that silently changes with the checkout policy is the
# same defect class the benchmark fixture copying was fixed for.
#
# Pin the text inputs to LF in the working tree, in every checkout.
benchmark/prompts/*.md text eol=lf
